#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341854 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04461982-533a-5e14-a19b-02276aebc7c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "352" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339156} {:answer/id #uuid "2e33a925-4daf-58c5-a21e-3d4f4217360d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339537} {:answer/id #uuid "3ecd2fc3-d4a8-52b9-9d61-7bc2eced0fd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "176" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339692} {:answer/id #uuid "71d46223-059f-51b1-a88d-cb76b966f2cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "110" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340141} {:answer/id #uuid "e92a6c3e-a51a-5f4a-85da-5de36c8fce2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "275" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04461982-533a-5e14-a19b-02276aebc7c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "352" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339156} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f5f87ca-efec-5b28-8dc7-45a1cc64fa5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e092bdb9-fca3-5ab8-88ef-c95e1a9b5b5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-72739" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(B)=11.$ What is the value of $det(2B)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot B)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=2$ and $n=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(2B) & ={2}^{5}\\cdot det(B) \\\\  & =32\\cdot 11 \\\\  & =352.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341855 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17922ecf-87f8-5af9-872a-3d5dc6da26af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339339} {:answer/id #uuid "3e3f2587-b4ad-5bf0-81b7-1df62ffb7a09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-243" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339686} {:answer/id #uuid "a21fdf0b-c950-5ec9-b67b-31a39827c266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340600} {:answer/id #uuid "ae1d7c41-28d1-55a3-9882-2c2b96500495" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340714} {:answer/id #uuid "f3da6cbc-6c90-5ed2-9aad-88c3625d3d86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-192" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3da6cbc-6c90-5ed2-9aad-88c3625d3d86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-192" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341277} :answer-field/id #uuid "ded707a6-03c1-52cc-8868-8933afddd3df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341773}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bce6072f-0fd1-50b6-a305-a94b72b85f4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-72740" :question/problem "Suppose $Y$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $det(Y)=-3.$ What is the value of $det(4Y)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot Y)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(Y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=4$ and $n=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(4Y) & ={4}^{3}\\cdot det(Y) \\\\  & =64\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-192.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341856 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "324c36d9-d587-5ad4-b856-b4a184318900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339571} {:answer/id #uuid "38399355-cd75-56b5-9d19-7d3f47ff3b69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339634} {:answer/id #uuid "8be69226-28da-50ff-98ec-1d3d59e714b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340381} {:answer/id #uuid "961b4655-5108-5d90-a218-c3ac9780ce82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340483} {:answer/id #uuid "cf9c387a-7e8e-5edc-8f1b-4a0bf8e4e535" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8be69226-28da-50ff-98ec-1d3d59e714b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340381} :answer-field/id #uuid "d175a015-4083-5d2d-b145-bf4b4fc1ec76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "31c24ae4-5a26-5d23-82f7-e8e80b937d7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-72752" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(B)=-10.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1}$ and ${R}_{4}↔{R}_{6}.$ What is the value of $det(C)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{4}↔{R}_{6}$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1}$ involves multiplying a row by $\\frac{1}{5},$ so the determinant is multiplied by $\\frac{1}{5}$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one and multiply by $\\frac{1}{5}$ as well. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (-det(B)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}det(B) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (-10) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342000 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e575bf2-282a-56e0-9c7b-f9d668c70fd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & -16 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340104} {:answer/id #uuid "81c756d9-3c31-59cb-a4e0-7950314357f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340296} {:answer/id #uuid "a1613f2b-9f40-56d7-b338-827222fcc89f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 12\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340591} {:answer/id #uuid "ca5a603a-0d9e-53c5-965d-695328e8649e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340920} {:answer/id #uuid "ce31b1b2-1883-577c-b531-35a7f77096b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -16 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340959}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca5a603a-0d9e-53c5-965d-695328e8649e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340920} :answer-field/id #uuid "d185127d-bb7a-5f18-8d05-fdf27c7419f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341748}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "99972d7b-41c2-573c-8100-907314a5a411" :question/math-academy-id "q-73524" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & -16 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 12 & -6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & -16 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 12 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 12 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342020 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d3cb3a6-9b25-5f14-b7fe-ef0f81082c39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=9$, $y=9$, and $z=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339832} {:answer/id #uuid "6637df9f-50f4-58dd-8cf1-2dded102c657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-166$, $y=-91$, and $z=-22$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340027} {:answer/id #uuid "82ffd466-0e67-5425-9c00-af468a2c3588" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-89$, $y=-47$, and $z=-11$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340306} {:answer/id #uuid "af2f918c-cf0f-5b21-8e87-4c608c0f9852" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-33$, $y=-15$, and $z=-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340724} {:answer/id #uuid "c76cf58e-617a-5441-8169-40443447226f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=142$, $y=85$, and $z=22$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6637df9f-50f4-58dd-8cf1-2dded102c657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-166$, $y=-91$, and $z=-22$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340027} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cf34cc2-5873-5eaf-970b-9dc56a73754a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4fabb78b-3a40-50c6-9149-8d79603a31f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-73579" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+6y-3z &=18 \\\\ -4x+8y-3z &=2 \\\\ y-4z &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & 6 & -3 & 18 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & 6 & -3 & 18 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -22 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -22 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -22\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+z &=-6 \\\\ y-4z &=-3 \\\\ z &=-22,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=-22$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-4(-22) &=-3\\,⟹\\,y=-91.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-91$ and $z=-22$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-2(-91)+(-22) &=-6\\,⟹\\,x=-166.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-166$, $y=-91$, and $z=-22.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342022 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08c85a87-f9d3-5992-bd65-769c46e1d92d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨11,-8,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339203} {:answer/id #uuid "0fbe2b87-90d4-5154-8a7b-4cbe5d76ee8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨39,-28,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339272} {:answer/id #uuid "266e54c3-4543-5283-9017-83d16e10e193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨25,-18,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339463} {:answer/id #uuid "32af4883-fe55-53ee-8722-a0f084a72e2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,2,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339575} {:answer/id #uuid "79208760-a400-5994-ac65-f0b5469feeb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-17,12,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fbe2b87-90d4-5154-8a7b-4cbe5d76ee8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨39,-28,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339272} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0944fb0-08b1-53ae-b7d8-bc6730da208f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341713}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3624bdf6-d1bf-5873-8a2a-1542d72f9250" :question/math-academy-id "q-73584" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y-2z &=3 \\\\ y+5z &=-8 \\\\ z &=4,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=4$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+5(4) &=-8\\,⟹\\,y=-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-28$ and $z=4$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(-28)-2(4) &=3\\,⟹\\,x=39.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=39$, $y=-28$, and $z=4.$ Or, in vector form $⟨39,-28,4⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342023 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f84b955-e25e-5955-8a2a-87d8b550463b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨52,21,-11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339543} {:answer/id #uuid "304cea0c-89a4-55c8-b0d0-dffbc12bb18b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339549} {:answer/id #uuid "35874527-0d05-510c-938e-52c64b49f406" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,-3,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339602} {:answer/id #uuid "57014e05-78ee-56aa-a36c-1a4147653d05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-58,-23,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339924} {:answer/id #uuid "e70f0c3f-b109-5746-a6d9-5b910dad1d5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,1,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57014e05-78ee-56aa-a36c-1a4147653d05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-58,-23,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339924} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5f662ab-5ce0-5cde-8194-11854041cc57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341727}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8a6417a9-7e20-54a9-9651-61368745cde5" :question/math-academy-id "q-73588" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 2 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 16 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 2 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 16 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 16 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 11\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+3z &=-2 \\\\ y+2z &=-1 \\\\ z &=11,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=11$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+2(11) &=-1\\,⟹\\,y=-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-23$ and $z=11$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(-23)+3(11) &=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-58.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-58$, $y=-23$, and $z=11.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨-58,-23,11⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342025 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "061b84d7-0a88-5827-a09a-0ae94645e28e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339179} {:answer/id #uuid "3493c0b1-471a-5165-b338-34b981a66bfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339595} {:answer/id #uuid "3670b23e-82b8-5a09-8d82-457c528c5b8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339614} {:answer/id #uuid "b35d9857-7680-5d0d-9437-cc48d8d3277a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340757} {:answer/id #uuid "bd407622-a505-57f5-ad35-f323345504ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340818}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "061b84d7-0a88-5827-a09a-0ae94645e28e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339179} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa4b0ec2-bc66-5a30-b57d-09c5803067da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341676}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7ecd0e17-9926-5c80-9527-2ab263ac9de2" :question/math-academy-id "q-73592" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-6y+3z &=-6 \\\\ 2x-4y+3z &=-1 \\\\ 2y-4z &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & -6 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & -6 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $2$nd row by $\\frac{1}{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342072 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48bee43f-e5d4-5fe4-ba44-cbfab244bb95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339776} {:answer/id #uuid "7cd77b81-1334-565d-8d3e-a2dd22d80c81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340253} {:answer/id #uuid "98819df0-6bd8-514f-987b-6451b9591fa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340501} {:answer/id #uuid "e19f3444-b301-5e49-b412-439b90466a1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2-3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341127} {:answer/id #uuid "eae4a6a8-5987-5a1e-bdd5-af1c44dee51c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eae4a6a8-5987-5a1e-bdd5-af1c44dee51c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341202} :answer-field/id #uuid "7801b1aa-c6e8-5bd6-8f4c-7fe9a4c707f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341591}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f00ce7fb-f804-52bb-ae27-0431b21c7460" :question/math-academy-id "q-73738" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=-2 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-3y=-2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-2+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2+3y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=⟨-2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342073 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c87faa6-b893-53ba-92f4-903ccf2dd32d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339374} {:answer/id #uuid "359295b0-82ba-5167-85b6-7dd0bfdb6bf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339603} {:answer/id #uuid "60eaf115-9b83-5456-8a7e-58465ef148d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339993} {:answer/id #uuid "64ccd9c1-b048-5406-90fe-2f5854979f7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340021} {:answer/id #uuid "6ac239fb-67c1-5152-911c-d8d3251c0f0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 16\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60eaf115-9b83-5456-8a7e-58465ef148d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339993} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b1f506b-8f53-50ce-aefc-1cc168e288d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9dd0d4fd-091a-5d63-898d-8efe81821dbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-73742" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -9 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -9 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342074 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e31a355-1c40-5d8a-9af0-19c5963ac08f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339393} {:answer/id #uuid "4cf92298-be3d-52f5-b6f4-979bddf4b7ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339828} {:answer/id #uuid "6fa3c7cb-67b7-55fa-a86f-b3ee447db5a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340119} {:answer/id #uuid "ebef8c1d-8feb-531f-8801-d33f9474093b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341206} {:answer/id #uuid "f41afd66-1114-59c9-af82-7a7d211334fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cf92298-be3d-52f5-b6f4-979bddf4b7ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339828} :answer-field/id #uuid "7df87fa2-2bdf-5af2-bcd5-28691af80256" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341601}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f7492471-0301-5306-8f40-5431247eb08f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73743" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342079 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35e6a7c5-5218-5d25-a8f6-7848a5bca3fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339610} {:answer/id #uuid "42fb3843-e811-598c-9cd8-40fa0350bea1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1+2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339713} {:answer/id #uuid "57cf24ad-e2ac-533d-8f71-64d4e595fa8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2-y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339928} {:answer/id #uuid "ad94e501-a2d3-5422-a57f-c8541c6ecb28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2+y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340708} {:answer/id #uuid "d21c64f6-9851-5d4c-8362-9495bc2b9f3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1-2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35e6a7c5-5218-5d25-a8f6-7848a5bca3fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339610} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0dcd427-5fab-5d80-85bc-c5c9b1007acd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341690}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b0b4636b-3357-5697-b846-0e6a1da3fd28" :question/math-academy-id "q-73751" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-10y &=-5 \\\\ 2x-4y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}5 & -10 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}5 & -10 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y &=4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=4$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=4,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342080 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "748a6c3f-5c5a-52d0-80b1-56ed7d055f93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340168} {:answer/id #uuid "8ab41392-7ec6-5d49-9a1b-01cc4e0b27b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3-5y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340369} {:answer/id #uuid "9fc2a610-a9e4-54f3-94d8-269cdee17d29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5-3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340572} {:answer/id #uuid "c22c25c6-e37d-5a37-9893-298241fa6efb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340856} {:answer/id #uuid "d1d9e052-394f-58fd-8671-dd57676a70e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3+5y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340988}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c22c25c6-e37d-5a37-9893-298241fa6efb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340856} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0f127f7-fee8-5dab-b7e7-c77e03e05e5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341692}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "824eec75-5ee7-5066-9e8b-de6f124de7ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-73752" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-6y &=10 \\\\ -x+3y &=-5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -6 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -6 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=5 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-3y=5.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=5+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5+3y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342110 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a0b569a-8def-5df5-b42f-3135dd4d5db0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339360} {:answer/id #uuid "3896821e-dec7-5884-ad52-5ca3a114b733" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339637} {:answer/id #uuid "3c9d29a7-85be-58bd-8990-c807b06606e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339668} {:answer/id #uuid "ab3c29be-4bcc-5dc0-b48a-fbfcfb942938" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340687} {:answer/id #uuid "db5099b6-1298-5164-b17c-d9086cd69a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3896821e-dec7-5884-ad52-5ca3a114b733" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339637} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbf00c01-ca7d-54b8-ace5-516180ba4620" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341767}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0a045a18-4b26-532b-8e6c-7d683732c9ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-73931" :question/problem "Find $x$, if $3a+2x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a+2x & =b \\\\ 2x & =b-3a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(b-3a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ x & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342111 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c413e0c-c33c-56fd-b3d6-1e2460eddd2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339817} {:answer/id #uuid "5fbea1da-ddb8-5da7-9356-26e81196486b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339981} {:answer/id #uuid "9dbf3a25-7be0-5074-837a-44451831d6fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -16 \\\\ 17\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340551} {:answer/id #uuid "b6ff64a2-c9dc-52e8-b2a7-08e6cc581675" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340782} {:answer/id #uuid "bb6ed45b-1d7b-51d7-a69f-8c508581247c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dbf3a25-7be0-5074-837a-44451831d6fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -16 \\\\ 17\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340551} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cc52df3-e394-5abf-ba0d-579bc781b63c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3b51a337-e5d6-556d-a72d-bef903a48688" :question/math-academy-id "q-73933" :question/problem "Find $x$, if $5a-3x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 18 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5a-3x & =b \\\\ 3x & =5a-b \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}(5a-b) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}(5\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 18 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -48 \\\\ 51\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ x & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -16 \\\\ 17\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342116 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19d8ca8c-8922-5497-b29f-07f42b1c0328" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339356} {:answer/id #uuid "225a0463-cbb8-5790-893a-13e777295f9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339423} {:answer/id #uuid "5a2860ef-3991-5816-8783-30dbaa549960" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339948} {:answer/id #uuid "88e4363d-a9d9-5e7c-8f3b-9118648894cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340350} {:answer/id #uuid "a3b0b254-d5ee-58ae-b3cb-ddf74a08a8e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a2860ef-3991-5816-8783-30dbaa549960" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339948} :answer-field/id #uuid "80a50f39-711b-58a4-835e-c4efbd2ce316" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341606}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0008ebd1-cf28-5d38-a9cd-5c6dde0f95a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-73951" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,d=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$\n." :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=-11 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAdding the second and the third  equations we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{1} & =-16\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{1}=-2$ into the third equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(-2)+{x}_{2} &=-5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting ${x}_{1}=-2$ and ${x}_{2}=3$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & =3 \\\\ (-2)+2(3) & =3 \\\\ 4 & =3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a false statement. \n\nSo, the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342117 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32d443f5-4a4c-51aa-af01-414ca3fa7326" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339577} {:answer/id #uuid "7176331f-77ce-5fd1-a3ac-5da0c1e2a04b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340136} {:answer/id #uuid "8b60455d-0f91-5c1b-b1a2-179e00d5ba83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340376} {:answer/id #uuid "c1c850a2-343b-5521-9ce1-8a561961b355" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340853} {:answer/id #uuid "f64a326f-5394-5da4-88ca-9fe93d38d48b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32d443f5-4a4c-51aa-af01-414ca3fa7326" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339577} :answer-field/id #uuid "d05bc05c-9d23-5ddd-9cf1-1346736f76da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341745}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "eec4fe83-c254-5d51-9484-b88391578898" :question/math-academy-id "q-73952" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=-7 \\\\ -{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAdding the first and the second equation we get\n\n$$\n-2{x}_{2}=-8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=4.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{2}=4$ into the first equation yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} & =-7 \\\\ {x}_{1}-(4) & =-7 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-7+4 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=4$ into the third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} & =6 \\\\ 2(-3)+3(4) & =6 \\\\ 6 & =6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=4,$ which means\n\n$$\n-3{a}_{1}+4{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-3+4=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342118 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fc79319-1174-5e30-8921-c2ddee82bff8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339273} {:answer/id #uuid "9fc2f746-79cb-5fe6-bb3f-959e15f530f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340573} {:answer/id #uuid "a4526df4-3faf-51d1-bf8d-80803e953d0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340621} {:answer/id #uuid "a8889610-4b78-5044-ae29-aded8c4e08c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340661} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e743ee-717a-5ee8-8be6-6df96ac57d49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fc2f746-79cb-5fe6-bb3f-959e15f530f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340573} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7acad01-3471-5823-b302-ef28c20fd009" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341731}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "abf235b3-2d59-5bfb-aea0-aa237461f6b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-73954" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -18\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -18\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-2{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}5{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -18\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -18\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} &=16 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} &=-18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $3$, the second equation by $2$, and adding the resulting equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15{x}_{2}+8{x}_{2} & =48-2 \\\\ 23{x}_{2} & =46 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=2$  into the second equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} & =-1\\text{ } \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+4(2) & =-1 \\\\ 3{x}_{1} & =-9 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=2$ into our third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} & =-18 \\\\ 4(-3)-3(2) & =-18 \\\\ -18 & =-18,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=2,$ which means\n\n$$\n-3{a}_{1}+2{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-3)+2=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id 