x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}4{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=7 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=9 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the third equation by $-1$ and adding the result to the first equation we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-3{x}_{1} & =7-4 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow,  we substitute ${x}_{1}=3$ into the third equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} & =4 \\\\ 3(3)-{x}_{2} & =4 \\\\ -{x}_{2} & =4-9 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=5$ into the second equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} & =9 \\\\ -2(3)+3(5) & =9 \\\\ -6+15 & =9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=5,$ which means\n\n$$\n3{a}_{1}+5{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3+5=8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342126 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3430db20-ef90-5054-8d8b-b6f798f4c553" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339592} {:answer/id #uuid "351054d6-ba57-5e06-82bb-d7c3e717e126" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339598} {:answer/id #uuid "bf850701-8c93-5374-9a42-dca7c25ca858" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340836} {:answer/id #uuid "cf811142-93c6-5d20-b217-29c2c57c680b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340975} {:answer/id #uuid "dbf87647-1ef7-5b76-85e7-37be4269b0ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "351054d6-ba57-5e06-82bb-d7c3e717e126" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339598} :answer-field/id #uuid "85f23f2c-e934-5f48-ab5a-edc1193c2c22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "33debd45-f90c-578d-9c6b-11c54937ac6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-73992" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{3} \\\\ 5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ 5{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=-5 \\\\ 5{x}_{3} &=-10 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -5 & 16\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -5 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2.5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2.5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=-5 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2.5\\,{x}_{3} &=8 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-2.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-2.5(-2)=8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=8-5=3.\n$$\n\nFinally,  substituting ${x}_{2}=3$ and ${x}_{3}=-2$  into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(3)+2(-2)=-5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=2$, ${x}_{2}=3$, and ${x}_{3}=-2,$ which means \n\n$$\n2{a}_{1}+3{a}_{2}-2{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2+3-2=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342130 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ca1e367-7e59-5b69-861b-8c5df685d98a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339240} {:answer/id #uuid "70e98200-2ef8-5fee-9135-1a64cdf08565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340130} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f91210-c308-5ac5-8b5f-ecea8232309c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340589} {:answer/id #uuid "cd78319b-964c-5a76-83e0-5cc4ba5b698b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340951} {:answer/id #uuid "d5c0ee9d-d678-5d90-ac70-ae36c44cd666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd78319b-964c-5a76-83e0-5cc4ba5b698b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340951} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6466acd-a8cc-51d2-bb7d-d48bfacf96c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341757}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ff5142a4-ab7b-5300-baa5-14f6253ed7fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-74006" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then   we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -{x}_{3} \\\\ -3{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-2 \\\\ -{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=5 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -12\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=-5 \\\\ 0 &=-12.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0=-12$  gives a false statement. So the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342132 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cd5d137-daee-5d6d-98d8-3497a80c61ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339245} {:answer/id #uuid "1d07c66f-c54f-5a22-89c4-35d7095387f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339379} {:answer/id #uuid "87f4b2e6-5682-5dda-9d57-6cd28ab535f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340346} {:answer/id #uuid "90e508ef-9eec-5c7a-8be0-834a65ad1d3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340427} {:answer/id #uuid "9316673f-9aac-5adc-b91d-046d54518f3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87f4b2e6-5682-5dda-9d57-6cd28ab535f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340346} :answer-field/id #uuid "2eff5ea8-b869-5727-bf8d-1f462e27220d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6ca28715-77ca-55f5-9aad-4851b6f70f79" :question/math-academy-id "q-74028" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=-1 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=-9 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=-1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=-3 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(-1)=-3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\nFinally, by substituting ${x}_{2}=-2,{x}_{3}=-1$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} & =-1 \\\\ {x}_{1}+(-2)+3(-1) & =-1 \\\\ {x}_{1}-5 & =-1 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=4$, ${x}_{2}=-2$, and ${x}_{3}=-1,$ which means \n\n$$\n4{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2}-{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=4+(-2)-(-1)=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342133 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dd1e2d3-3d25-597c-a847-faa140432c9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339255} {:answer/id #uuid "28a2b981-6db8-5f16-b21b-6ae088a23e3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339484} {:answer/id #uuid "309c51a6-6646-55e5-a9ef-db0cd36bd5b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339553} {:answer/id #uuid "732f8930-5de1-53c0-8f9f-0564fc2ea176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340149} {:answer/id #uuid "d7a94670-179b-5241-8088-b40d00d22100" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "309c51a6-6646-55e5-a9ef-db0cd36bd5b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339553} :answer-field/id #uuid "95f0dc3f-6280-5dbc-ad92-0375cafd9b79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "237520c7-3369-5c34-87a7-ba4be3c9b705" :question/math-academy-id "q-74032" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{3} \\\\ -11{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-11{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=5 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-11{x}_{3} &=-18 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -15 & -30\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{15}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=5 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} &=-6 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this value into  the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-2(2)=-6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, by substituting ${x}_{2}=-2$ and ${x}_{3}=2$ into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1}+(-2)+3(2) & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1}+4 & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=1$, ${x}_{2}=-2$, and ${x}_{3}=2,$ which means \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2}+2{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1+(-2)+2=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342134 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c3b744a-01a9-54ce-8529-5a08f78940d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339816} {:answer/id #uuid "60e09ff1-d3cc-58ef-8987-5a5f148e2536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339992} {:answer/id #uuid "8a3631e7-ceb5-57d9-884a-4e22407dcb9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340363} {:answer/id #uuid "9ad3c54b-5811-537d-84b5-61c05d4666df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340526} {:answer/id #uuid "a932259c-57be-54ad-a6fe-9cb2e6f3f068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a932259c-57be-54ad-a6fe-9cb2e6f3f068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340667} :answer-field/id #uuid "84898483-2191-5459-b5c9-62b59dd71df8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "118e9ea0-84b3-5e8f-866f-104da032b6d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-74035" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=-3 \\\\ 5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=4 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0.2 & 0.8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=-{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0.2 & 0.8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=-3 \\\\ {x}_{2}+\\,0.2{x}_{3} &=0.8 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+0.2(-1)=0.8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\n   \n\nFinally,  substituting ${x}_{2}=1$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(1)=-3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-2.\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-2$, ${x}_{2}=1$, and ${x}_{3}=-1,$ which means  \n\n$$\n-2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}-{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2+1-1=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342138 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11e315df-67b1-5a51-8722-8b611d6b4f04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339284} {:answer/id #uuid "63215e56-f763-5d47-ad93-5bf665123767" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340010} {:answer/id #uuid "cb20f6ae-be9d-53d3-9a62-422bcfb9533a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340927} {:answer/id #uuid "e2f1ab45-f348-545f-bf2c-ba9c88f197d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341136} {:answer/id #uuid "f0ac09fc-fbae-5dfd-bb2b-94215e0d375c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341248}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0ac09fc-fbae-5dfd-bb2b-94215e0d375c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341248} :answer-field/id #uuid "f04b6cf2-abe9-50ed-8eee-447e512fcc60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341811}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a8d414ab-92e5-5218-83d9-6fd3ed558d87" :question/math-academy-id "q-74046" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3} &=8 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} &=-6 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -14\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & -20\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3} &=8 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} &=-6 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=5.$ Substituting this value in the second and first equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{2}-2(5)=-6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=4 \\\\  & {x}_{1}+5=8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=3$, ${x}_{2}=4$, and ${x}_{3}=5,$ which means \n\n$$\n3{a}_{1}+4{a}_{2}+5{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=3+4+5=12.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345006 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "499ee1f6-801f-57f7-aab7-474f9d374084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342844} {:answer/id #uuid "7f5bfdd1-ee64-5fd7-9c47-3b4c4e1a2370" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343334} {:answer/id #uuid "89079bb4-c6f6-5b1d-be0d-68fe5c1822de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343425} {:answer/id #uuid "b1061a87-039d-51d8-ba91-e57582fc2d4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343791} {:answer/id #uuid "de0e2b5b-97e2-5bfc-aeeb-9c68939e0ca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89079bb4-c6f6-5b1d-be0d-68fe5c1822de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343425} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3d7b3da-d4d8-5800-9823-61684cbd00d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3a38bfe9-93f0-569e-b890-07afd16179a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-74972" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},$ and ${a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find a basis of $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$  by inspection." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a basis of $S$ is a set of linearly independent vectors that spans $S.$\n\nFrom the given vectors, we can see that ${a}_{2}$ is a linear combination of vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=2\\cdot {a}_{1}+0\\cdot {a}_{3}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the vector ${a}_{2}$ can be removed from $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ without changing the span. So $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is spanned by just ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}}.$ \n\nLastly, note that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent since they are not parallel. So the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set that spans $S.$\n\nTherefore, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB={\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{{a}_{1}},\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}}_{{a}_{3}}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345007 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0129cbdd-ad02-50ee-b5f7-bf8f408c1f5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342255} {:answer/id #uuid "2c9ca248-4869-5b0b-bc00-4d367d28db90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342612} {:answer/id #uuid "c750272e-2b00-59a7-82e5-28f9217d90c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343987} {:answer/id #uuid "ee42860a-5869-55a2-ae25-e3c37b1186df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344333} {:answer/id #uuid "f7c313e7-823b-59ff-bb5e-400080c9fcb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0129cbdd-ad02-50ee-b5f7-bf8f408c1f5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342255} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d977d8c-2f49-5bcd-b94a-def80a7ada93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344542}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "36ba20d1-68b8-5338-a56b-78cf02075d33" :question/math-academy-id "q-74973" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},$ and ${a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find a basis of $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ by inspection." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a basis of $S$ is a set of linearly independent vectors that spans $S.$\n\nFrom the given vectors, we can see that ${a}_{2}$ is a linear combination of vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=2\\cdot {a}_{1}+0\\cdot {a}_{3}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the vector ${a}_{2}$ can be removed from $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ without changing the span. So $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is spanned by just ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}}.$ \n\nLastly, note that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent since they are not parallel. So the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set that spans $S.$\n\nTherefore, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB={\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{{a}_{1}},\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{{a}_{3}}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345008 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ab4781e-438b-5348-99ff-eec3eb4e0100" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343293} {:answer/id #uuid "cfa30883-6751-55c6-b0ee-fe2f697d5ba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344063} {:answer/id #uuid "d766a2df-5fbb-553e-b26c-26f93187db41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344131} {:answer/id #uuid "efb373b6-5224-59a4-a7a4-bdc6d2e7a6af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344345} {:answer/id #uuid "fa8ef4f5-53a3-5d84-970e-d479db1efe89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "efb373b6-5224-59a4-a7a4-bdc6d2e7a6af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344345} :answer-field/id #uuid "39b4cfc5-a4ba-51a4-9c05-61c7cbe36acb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344592}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d8b8f1bc-6448-59a2-9a5e-90acf024211c" :question/math-academy-id "q-74979" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},$ ${a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix},$ and ${a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a subset of linearly independent vectors. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 12 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 16 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 16 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one.\n\nThe $1$st and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB={\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345009 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15706f7d-fa4e-5373-8ab0-28f245b1898a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342428} {:answer/id #uuid "388ffd1b-44a7-5b05-aeb3-9ea87351970c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342703} {:answer/id #uuid "8dc1b14a-1842-5451-91f0-d0429d1f4f5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343478} {:answer/id #uuid "a162d6e2-b381-5358-8f39-dcf7857f91d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343661} {:answer/id #uuid "d90780cc-a7e2-537c-8faa-7ba7f8342821" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344143}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "388ffd1b-44a7-5b05-aeb3-9ea87351970c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342703} :answer-field/id #uuid "33972fe3-e2f1-5e4c-bd15-6ed0222bd9fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344584}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0e4db7b3-e6f9-5f5c-a603-6b52766bfd31" :question/math-academy-id "q-74981" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},$ ${a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},$ and ${a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a subset of linearly independent vectors. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, our matrix is already in a row echelon form.\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $2$nd columns are pivot columns, while the $3$rd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nThe $1$st and $2$nd columns from the original matrix are ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB={\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345028 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15f78aa7-ba0f-5d13-846d-fbc94e2afa95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=2{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342432} {:answer/id #uuid "241a24a7-5f82-525f-ad03-f16375090dea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342540} {:answer/id #uuid "6dd283e5-269e-5f5a-a0fd-7a2a835aed07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343183} {:answer/id #uuid "d655a135-5e27-5248-bddf-205d3acacdab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344116} {:answer/id #uuid "f7886d15-508e-5b11-9ed7-9f9faa927e9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dd283e5-269e-5f5a-a0fd-7a2a835aed07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343183} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7cf27c3-db5e-5369-a028-e09189594c1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "eeb8f8cc-b741-5d2f-aec0-2320813ea3a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-75109" :question/problem "Consider $E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." :question/worked-solution "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the first row of ${I}_{3}$ and adding $2$ times the third row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345037 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1151bec1-be5e-52e9-91d5-7d7fc2d0a0e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342389} {:answer/id #uuid "529d62e4-81fa-5367-ac0b-c57031f84a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342925} {:answer/id #uuid "9ca238c5-28f7-5de0-b397-9bd6e2d481d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343619} {:answer/id #uuid "a99f528e-cf8f-52e6-b044-e7cea44ec1f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343733} {:answer/id #uuid "c37c5619-a1d6-5644-82ff-d5f8b870c069" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1151bec1-be5e-52e9-91d5-7d7fc2d0a0e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342389} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1faebe9-3606-5dbb-ae69-d4fddcb1c6d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e88238aa-13fb-5633-8c2c-6d50b88f64f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-75164" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:=-9{R}_{3},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{3}:=-9{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :=-9{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345042 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13f63618-8846-5383-aae6-4dbaaf8b19f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342413} {:answer/id #uuid "3e30f118-5a78-53e9-a1ef-b9644cb5a0ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342750} {:answer/id #uuid "41c335d3-ab39-5b8b-859c-8b87612e9ca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342777} {:answer/id #uuid "47e207db-d162-5b2a-aabc-04c06199aec4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342832} {:answer/id #uuid "9b36de3a-b505-5603-aad8-74e749f4e5f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343608}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e30f118-5a78-53e9-a1ef-b9644cb5a0ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342750} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c55726b-9c40-57f3-8435-1d4f7d77ea3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344619}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0854eeb0-38e4-505f-a728-28edf544308c" :question/math-academy-id "q-75192" :question/problem "What is the inverse of the elementary matrix \n$$\n\\displaystyle B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $B$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|ccc}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] &  & {R}_{2}:=3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|ccc}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse is obtained on the right-hand side of our big matrix after the transformation. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{B}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345054 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e091203-25ce-5885-9770-1af02d89c1a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 23 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342881} {:answer/id #uuid "8038a03e-f655-597c-a25e-0761af025e42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343340} {:answer/id #uuid "87687715-c77e-54e5-b787-22c79fe01b64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 23 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343409} {:answer/id #uuid "b61dd69b-2fbd-5e2a-a606-160cf442dae3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 23 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343833} {:answer/id #uuid "fad7b41c-614d-55e2-a3d4-0745e909bb52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 23 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fad7b41c-614d-55e2-a3d4-0745e909bb52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 23 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344445} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fd02e6c-249e-5581-b354-6d760a65a896" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344547}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b3d9954a-235f-5dbc-876a-c24dd6400de2" :question/math-academy-id "q-75239" :question/problem "Find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{E}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -23 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${E}_{1}$ and ${E}_{2}$ are both elementary matrices.\n\nFirst, we need to find ${E}_{2}^{-1}.$ We write down ${E}_{2}$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{2}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|ccc}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -23 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+23{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|ccc}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 23 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{E}_{2}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 23 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}:$ \n\n$$\n{E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 23 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 23 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345087 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "005d0dc0-c679-52c6-abbc-b50e1a9c606d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342245} {:answer/id #uuid "1bade1d0-68d0-5f74-9071-e51229d51e1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342473} {:answer/id #uuid "23ad34dd-4dce-5431-b238-8e2f933f2ad9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342535} {:answer/id #uuid "24307cfa-00ed-5caf-8cf9-ec8ae54f022f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342544} {:answer/id #uuid "d8d586e1-9945-5f53-ab4a-d3dcc0dca9aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bade1d0-68d0-5f74-9071-e51229d51e1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342473} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8c0cc2e-b502-5e16-85dd-960d484ba8bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344929}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "062bb064-038f-55e1-92f0-0d30d2ec231e" :question/math-academy-id "q-75472" :question/problem "Calculate the product ${I}_{2}G$ given that ${I}_{2}$ is the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix and\n$$\n\\displaystyle G=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix ${I}_{2}$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $G$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\n{I}_{2}\\cdot G=G=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345088 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "100dd380-18b7-591d-be6c-89c73e6809d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342377} {:answer/id #uuid "515f51d6-c508-5850-8fe3-dab670b624f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342911} {:answer/id #uuid "858cdfc9-2899-58cb-913d-c588d6653820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343383} {:answer/id #uuid "d3c49d8f-10f4-5a31-b6c4-c1e8fc3eb675" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344098} {:answer/id #uuid "f8a18937-b3a8-5fc5-ab9f-9c054f7cba2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "100dd380-18b7-591d-be6c-89c73e6809d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342377} :answer-field/id #uuid "15858fcb-aa80-596c-a531-08e6c8a9a97c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ae364f6e-5a7d-5d28-b89b-7967cff2127c" :question/math-academy-id "q-75473" :question/problem "Calculate the product $J{I}_{2}$ given that ${I}_{2}$ is the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix and\n$$\n\\displaystyle J=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix $J$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and ${I}_{2}$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\nJ\\cdot {I}_{2}=J=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}]}
